<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>The matrix <m>M = {\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -1 \\ 3 &amp; 2 \end{array}\right]}</m> maps triangle ABC, with <m>A({-2},\,{-1})</m>, <m>B({-2},\,{-3})</m> and <m>C({4},\,{4})</m>, onto triangle <m>A'B'C'</m>.</p><p>Find <m>A'</m>, <m>B'</m> and <m>C'</m>. Write them as the columns of a <m>2 \times 3</m> matrix, in the order <m>A'</m>, <m>B'</m>, <m>C'</m>.</p><div><fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Write the vertices as the columns of the object matrix and multiply by <m>M</m>. Each column of the answer is the image of the vertex in that column.</p><p><m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -1 \\ 3 &amp; 2 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{ccc} -2 &amp; -2 &amp; 4 \\ -1 &amp; -3 &amp; 4 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{ccc} 1 &amp; 3 &amp; -4 \\ -8 &amp; -12 &amp; 20 \end{array}\right]}</m></p><p>For A: <m>{\left[\begin{array}{cc} 0 &amp; -1 \\ 3 &amp; 2 \end{array}\right]}{\left[\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ -1 \end{array}\right]} = {\left[\begin{array}{c} 1 \\ -8 \end{array}\right]}</m>, since the top row gives <m>x' = {-y}</m> and the bottom row gives <m>y' = {2 y+3 x}</m>. So <m>A'</m> is <m>({1},\,{-8})</m>, <m>B'</m> is <m>({3},\,{-12})</m> and <m>C'</m> is <m>({-4},\,{20})</m>.</p><p>Sketch both triangles on squared paper to check: the origin O does not move under any matrix.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left[\begin{array}{ccc} 1 &amp; 3 &amp; -4 \\ -8 &amp; -12 &amp; 20 \end{array}\right]</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>